      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Cancer patients occasionally experience periods of rapidly escalating pain--\"crescendo\" pain--that may present a challenge in assessment and management. Although these episodes are often associated with progressive neoplasm, any of a variety of other processes may be involved. Delirium is a potentially treatable and frequently unrecognized factor. We present three patients who illustrate this relationship between delirium and a crescendo pattern of cancer pain."},
